games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "31058"} "1996"] "\n" [:option {:value "31149"} "2000"] "\n" [:option {:value "31258"} "2004"] "\n" [:option {:value "258676"} "2008"] "\n" [:option {:value "306000"} "2012"] "\n" [:option {:value "354218"} "2016"] "\n" [:option {:value "19001777"} "2020"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/158"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Beach Volleyball, Women" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "27 July –  9 August 2024"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/2172"} "Eiffel Tower Stadium (Champ de Mars), Paris, France"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/2002267"} "48 from 17 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Format"] [:td {:colspan "2"} "Top 16 teams from round-robin pools advanced to the single-elimination tournament."]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "Twenty-four teams, consisting of 48 athletes from 17 NOCs, competed in the event, although the Americans " [:a {:href "/athletes/126600"} "April Ross"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/147155"} "Alix Klineman"] " were not present and did not defend their gold medal."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The 17 highest-ranked eligible women’s pairs secured a direct spot for Paris 2024 based on the FIVB Olympic ranking points accrued in the 12 best performances from 1 January 2023 to 9 June 2024. The top five ranked teams were as follows: #1 – Brazil – " [:a {:href "/athletes/2101332"} "Duda Lisboa"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/2101333"} "Ana Patrícia Ramos"] ", the 2023 World silver medalists; #2 – the USA – " [:a {:href "/athletes/155370"} "Kristen Nuss"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/155373"} "Taryn Kloth"] ", the 2023 World bronze medalists; #3 – the other American team, " [:a {:href "/athletes/155372"} "Sara Hughes"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/147156"} "Kelly Cheng"] ", the 2023 World Champions; #4 – Canada with " [:a {:href "/athletes/141375"} "Melissa Humana-Paredes"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/141374"} "Brandie Wilkerson"] " (Humana-Paredes previously competed with " [:a {:href "/athletes/129435"} "Sarah Pavan"] ", notably winning the gold medal at the 2019 World Championships and two Commonwealth Games titles in 2018 and 2022); and #5 – the second Brazilian team – " [:a {:href "/athletes/155192"} "Carol Solberg"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/129248"} "Bárbara Seixas"] ". In 2015, Seixas and her partner " [:a {:href "/athletes/129247"} "Ágatha Rippel"] " had won gold at the 2015 World Championships. All these five top ranked teams, plus the French team of " [:a {:href "/athletes/2101733"} "Lézana Placette"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/2101734"} "Alexia Richard"] ", were top seeded in the draw of the six pools."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In the preliminary round, there was only one big surprise to report, as the top-seeded Canadian team of Melissa and Brandie lost 2 of their 3 matches and only qualified for the Round of 16 after winning their lucky loser match against the Czechs " [:a {:href "/athletes/129846"} "Barbora Hermannová"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/155218"} "Marie-Sára Štochlová"] ". The top seeded French team of " [:a {:href "/athletes/2101733"} "Lézana Placette"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/2101734"} "Alexia Richard"] " ranked third in pool F after 1 win and 2 losses, but were later defeated in the lucky loser match by the Japanese team of " [:a {:href "/athletes/155282"} "Akiko Hasegawa"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/144333"} "Miki Ishii"] "."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The Brazilians Duda and Ana Patrícia lost only two sets, one in the semi-finals against Australia, and the other in the final against the Melissa and Brandie duo, defeating them 26–24, 12–21, 15–10, for the gold medal. The Swiss team of " [:a {:href "/athletes/146636"} "Tanja Hüberli"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/146635"} "Nina Betschart-Brunner"] " won the bronze medal by defeating the Australians " [:a {:href "/athletes/128970"} "Mariafe Artacho"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/128972"} "Taliqua Clancy"] "."] "\n"] [:button {:id "button12248", :class "btn btn-default"} "Details"] [:script {} "$('#button12248').click(splits)"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Games Played", :class "split", :style "display: none"} "GP"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Wins"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Losses"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Points"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Sets"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Set Ratio"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Points"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Points Ratio"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Service Attempts"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Service In-Play"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Service Faults"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Service Aces"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Fastest Serve"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Attack Attempts"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Attack Successes"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Attack Errors"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Attack In-Play"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Block Successes"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Opponent Errors"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Dig Successes"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th 